-- MANUAL TEMPLATE ONLY. This file is inert when passed to psql and is not a migration.
-- Do not uncomment or schedule until the hosted IAM, Vault, Edge Runtime path,
-- plan limits, index readiness, and controlled end-to-end test are approved.
--
-- Proposed conservative cadence: 1 event every 10 minutes, after at most 100
-- outbox documents are examined in 4 stable pages. This creates 144 invocations/day
-- (4,320 per 30-day month), before any other Edge Function usage. At saturation,
-- one event normally performs a claim and acknowledgement (288 writes/day), and
-- checkpoint acquire/advance adds up to 288 writes/day: about 576 Firestore writes/day
-- excluding retries and other writers. Reads/retries and existing project traffic
-- also consume Firestore free quota. Recalculate with measured workload before activation.
-- Reads/retries and existing project traffic also consume Firestore free quota.
-- Recalculate with real workload and account-wide plan usage before activation.
--
-- Preconditions to verify manually:
--   * Hosted plan/project supports pg_cron, pg_net, Vault, and the required Edge Function.
--   * pgcrypto is installed in schema `extensions` and `extensions.hmac` is executable.
--   * Vault contains these exact names, separately provisioned through an approved
--     secret-management path (never put their values in Git or SQL history):
--       catalog_consumer_project_url       https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
--       catalog_consumer_publishable_key   public publishable/anon API key
--       catalog_consumer_hmac_secret       random secret with 32-256 UTF-8 bytes
--   * The function's `verify_jwt = false` is intentional only because the handler
--     verifies HMAC. `apikey` is a public gateway key, not authorization.
--   * A local runtime test confirms request.url.pathname equals the path signed below.
--   * The function is configured with `CATALOG_CONSUMER_ENABLED=true` and valid
--     server-side credentials. The local default remains disabled.
--
-- Every executable line below is deliberately commented. Review and copy only
-- after the preconditions and a hosted test have been approved.
